    task: "Read this extract from a newspaper column: 'Public money should be spent on hospitals, roads and schools, not on theatres, museums and art galleries. Art is a pleasant extra, and anyone who truly values it can pay for it.' Write a letter to the editor (200–250 words) responding to this opinion. Say what you are responding to, give your own view and support it with reasons. Use at least three expressions of certainty or hedging, such as 'It would appear that…', 'almost certainly' or 'I am convinced that…'.",
    taskAr: "قرأتَ في عمود صحفي رأياً يقول إن الأموال العامة يجب أن تُنفَق على المستشفيات والطرق والمدارس لا على المسارح والمتاحف ومعارض الفن، وإن الفن إضافة لطيفة يستطيع من يقدّره أن يدفع ثمنها بنفسه. اكتب رسالة إلى رئيس التحرير (200–250 كلمة) تردّ فيها على هذا الرأي: وضّح ما الذي تردّ عليه، واذكر موقفك، وادعمه بأسباب. استعمل ثلاث عبارات على الأقل من عبارات اليقين أو التحوّط (مثل It would appear that… وalmost certainly وI am convinced that…).",
    words: [200, 250],
    model: [
      "Dear Editor,",
      "I am writing in response to Mr Nasser's column, 'Culture We Cannot Afford', published on 3 March. I would like to take issue with his claim that public funding of the arts is a luxury, and I shall argue that the opposite is closer to the truth.",
      "It would appear that the writer regards the arts as mere entertainment. However, a public museum, theatre or music school offers far more than a pleasant evening. It gives children whose families cannot pay for private lessons their first chance to paint, play or perform, which might suggest that cultural funding is a form of education rather than decoration. Moreover, such places almost certainly attract visitors who spend money in nearby cafés and shops, so part of the investment returns to the community.",
      "I do not dispute that hospitals and schools are vital. Nevertheless, the two aims need not compete, since the sums spent on the arts are usually small compared with the national budget. Cutting them would save little while causing lasting damage, and if the state withdraws, only wealthy patrons will remain, and the arts will then serve the few rather than the many.",
      "I am convinced that a society which stops supporting its artists also stops imagining its own future. I therefore urge your readers, and the authorities, to protect public funding for the arts.",
      "Yours faithfully,",
      "Layla Barakat"
    ],
